{"h": {"measure": "A", "k": 20}, "sp": "nb", "rep": 101, "hyps": [{"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "skip_connect", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Adding the input-output residual where none exists gives large gains (exps 3,4) versus no change when skip is already there."}, {"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Filling an empty edge 3 with a conv helps (exp 12) while replacing an existing skip with a conv hurts (exp 11)."}, {"edit_edge": 4, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "Without the edge-3 path, removing edge 4 removes most remaining routes to the output and accuracy collapses (exp 7 vs 8)."}, {"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "skip_connect", "direction": "lower", "why": "Removing an existing skip from edge 3 costs several points (exps 19,20), whereas when edge 3 is already none the edit is a no-op."}, {"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 1, "cond_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "direction": "higher", "why": "Edge 5 only carries signal if node 2 receives input, and edge 1 is node 2's direct input (exp 2 vs 1)."}, {"edit_edge": 0, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 4, "cond_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "direction": "higher", "why": "A conv into node 1 is only useful when node 1's output reaches the output node, as through edge 4 (exp 6 vs 5)."}, {"edit_edge": 4, "edit_op": "nor_conv_1x1", "cond_edge": 0, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "If edge 0 is none, node 1 has no input, so adding an operation on edge 4 carries nothing (exp 17 vs 18)."}, {"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "avg_pool_3x3", "cond_edge": 5, "cond_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "direction": "lower", "why": "Replacing a learnable conv with parameter-free pooling loses capacity (exp 13), unlike filling an empty edge (exp 14)."}, {"edit_edge": 4, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 0, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "highe